#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161776 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161984 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e62e458d-0724-5dbe-b448-b79404f279f9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices of Quadratic Forms"}] :question/id #uuid "122fd33e-5ef4-5200-9c72-67f40f3b8ca0" :question/math-academy-id "e-8168" :question/problem "Which of the following could be matrices of quadratic forms defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2?$\n\n![](images/e5/e51c52e07d49052f578138e5c1d7e9f84a95ba8c454e7fcf834dcc9047dad432.png)" :question/worked-solution "Recall that every quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2$ has an associated $2 \\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $L$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2$ since it's a $3 \\times 3$ matrix (not $2 \\times 2$).\n\n- $M$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2.$  Although it's a $2 \\times 2$ matrix, $M$ is not symmetric since $m_{12} \\neq m_{21}.$\n\n- $N$ could be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on $\\mathbb{R}^2$ since it is a $2 \\times 2$ symmetric matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$N$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161777 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161985 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90f62dc8-396d-5f7f-8295-2e7b5d62bd78" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Quadratic Form"}] :question/id #uuid "d782c826-1111-5c83-98b6-220856d74b41" :question/math-academy-id "e-8169" :question/problem "![](images/79/791b214858b7ff88b6ad1ba98ea8336abbd678ffb34751b041e11cec8cd44143.png)\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the quadratic form $Q(\\mathbf{x}) = \\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{x}$ when ![](images/b7/b7df527ba563debac29dbdd838aadb4f219653a77077b70b65bdbfe579e26a0a.png)" :question/worked-solution "Substituting ![](images/1a/1a8e02bec4af0b88d7fa0f4cd87b9e0f89757ca87f494e1451650ac4f3a06dcf.png) into the expression for $Q(\\mathbf{x}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 23\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =86.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161778 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161986 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Quadratic Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/id #uuid "f3be44df-f059-5e92-b279-644fe1eb0985" :question/math-academy-id "e-8170" :question/problem "![](images/59/59d795aef27f3ae7598e1a8503ba0dbde377486b355e0db6decc4753f9ae7544.png)\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which expression represents the corresponding quadratic form $\\mathbf{x}^T \\! A \\mathbf{x}$ in terms of the components of ![](images/31/31a4a301bddfd7435f188f76c1702beb7c2eea01a1b174d5195f321cfdef3103.png)" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry $a_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term $a_{ij}x_i x_j$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =-1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(1){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(1){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+-1{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}({x}_{1}-{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161779 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161987 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form"}] :question/id #uuid "9ed75397-5920-5326-a5b9-7537e30f0a85" :question/math-academy-id "e-8171" :question/problem "![](images/1b/1bd9859db9b628b26d250310d38222e8d1474cbfa8d5d991217dc74d04e3f47d.png)\nThe matrix of the quadratic form ![](images/d4/d4ecb15785c7b91e8596dd5ee6d5f4f37bf8021c5be668ec618955d401d4818f.png) is given above. What is the value of ![](images/50/5076087e153b1b98d9b1798601bd9f4fb4858085d9fd7b5695ee28d0ec82383c.png)" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n![](images/86/8645c292302b7edfc416cf5ca509325a6ee9381fb231a7f2b159803b4dfda807.png)\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must do the following splits:\n\n- we split the coefficient of ![](images/df/dfb385bea2635645b1f9c86af71eff0dce97a954417745dbd38490f018f08e0a.png) between the entries ![](images/6a/6a348fce74db828ec978c7e135e99593bc998bfabecec36ecaf759cc06dba537.png) and\n\n- we split the coefficient of ![](images/0c/0ce406288d4b63c3156067f4ff753a5fec13d4461f11cf58252a1361f16b6911.png) between the entries ![](images/c2/c24c0fe76b0f877030d6130109d0b82ef187e05be9c103d8b913b9c3eb654200.png)\n\nSo, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n![](images/e8/e8fda0676083681fa61f11e26ca5455e06cf93ce11b657f7e1b46be3c30ff899.png)\n\nTherefore, ![](images/29/29e111e47c4fb83d1a5be9b51f83e463770c5c5d7a99eae453281f617e34fe86.png) ![](images/d6/d6faa78e35bd56fb2a138698ca72569d54c7da3305c3bb5b9dfafd8662d49d7a.png) and ![](images/a8/a8c65541492f0454624e520d1b86952208a1206735718dd49b7455f003d2bce5.png) Finally, \n![](images/85/851f6d6822dca779fa17406a68c7e6fbce37cf2642ce5994f8e95ede41e31921.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161984 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e62e458d-0724-5dbe-b448-b79404f279f9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices of Quadratic Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "355ee90c-29a8-5f7d-9858-d5d774afc427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464144} {:answer/id #uuid "52c13329-ed29-5a6a-9c3a-980f9b642801" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "355ee90c-29a8-5f7d-9858-d5d774afc427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464144} :answer-field/id #uuid "57268d9e-f878-521e-88c1-e38ad05c4b25" :answer-field/key "R" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465006} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fca2a6a-5f0e-57c2-b88a-83793aa0ea03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464146} {:answer/id #uuid "d9140ca1-8724-5815-b59d-81a85f001cf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464147}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fca2a6a-5f0e-57c2-b88a-83793aa0ea03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464146} :answer-field/id #uuid "d672360c-79a2-53e5-89fd-18eb4ebb73b0" :answer-field/key "S" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465007} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "729a3d56-7c5c-50c8-b093-a5ba7c6c0128" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464148} {:answer/id #uuid "a192252a-3f86-5dc5-852c-3bafb620daf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464149}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a192252a-3f86-5dc5-852c-3bafb620daf8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464149} :answer-field/id #uuid "045f8e77-8eca-5ea2-86b3-e877ff4aa8cc" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186465008}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d68a509c-d790-5483-ab3b-63aef29c3b19" :question/math-academy-id "q-140870" :question/problem "Which of the following could be matrices of quadratic forms defined on ${R}^{3}?$\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}],\\,S=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}],\\,T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that every quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ has an associated $3\\times 3$ symmetric matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $R$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ since it's a $2\\times 2$ matrix (not $3\\times 3$).\n\n- $S$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}.$ Although it's a $3\\times 3$ matrix, $S$ is not symmetric since ${s}_{23}\\ne {s}_{32}.$\n\n- $T$ could be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ since it is a $3\\times 3$ symmetric matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$T$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272171 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161986 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Quadratic Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a0f2148-7ade-5ec8-ab86-c7e431d919fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269940} {:answer/id #uuid "5ffb9214-474e-5372-a1eb-174b26aa7439" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}^{2}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270117} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4c2346-7df9-5410-9d87-366e1e19b329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270681} {:answer/id #uuid "dd9b028c-108b-526f-a4e8-1e7cb18ddf10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271214} {:answer/id #uuid "e0ae9565-9694-58a6-aab9-151038d2b131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271244}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f4c2346-7df9-5410-9d87-366e1e19b329" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270681} :answer-field/id #uuid "065e2a25-744f-55d4-9b51-be1e062d5b85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271514}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d5a533cc-6fd5-51dd-a1d8-7511844d6151" :question/math-academy-id "q-140928" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-1){x}_{1}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+(-1){x}_{3}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1}-{x}_{3})+{x}_{2}(3{x}_{3})+{x}_{3}(-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+6{x}_{2}{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161985 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90f62dc8-396d-5f7f-8295-2e7b5d62bd78" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03315f4c-29f9-5335-bf32-1a4c56087564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269297} {:answer/id #uuid "7c208796-7c48-534f-b951-cdeb5025345e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270358} {:answer/id #uuid "8c6dfe0c-feda-5664-9df0-54ac9c230c90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270488} {:answer/id #uuid "92037151-e69a-5500-b6e8-690e4fe8c09c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270544} {:answer/id #uuid "9c96fb7b-b378-527b-a9cb-ae21c483e8bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "03315f4c-29f9-5335-bf32-1a4c56087564" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "21" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269297} :answer-field/id #uuid "685add4a-af6c-5961-9669-2663c3076fb1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271697}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "95eb1ba0-88cc-5104-bc0d-3a93ab6de4cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-140929" :question/problem "Consider the quadratic form \n$Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{x}_{3}.$ \nEvaluate $Q(x)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "We are given that \n\n$$\nx=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the expression for $Q(x)$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-3{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={3}^{2}-4\\cdot 3\\cdot (-1)+2\\cdot 3\\cdot 0-3\\cdot (-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =9+12+0+0 \\\\  & =21.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161987 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09186c66-3df7-5958-bab9-d6eceedcf24b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269352} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc9401d-5750-5d84-973f-2999e18b0e40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269498} {:answer/id #uuid "43ef2164-f9ee-520c-ad40-88d74fa2b378" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269883} {:answer/id #uuid "4d695520-7dd1-5bf7-a0f0-916f7513d13d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269969} {:answer/id #uuid "5dddb6f7-c5c2-5d95-b52f-aa67277d9998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270103}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5dddb6f7-c5c2-5d95-b52f-aa67277d9998" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270103} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fa92d2a-c490-5653-aff1-56f027732c5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271655}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bcdcd1b6-5a07-5e6a-b243-0a76c6534f4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-140932" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ b & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =2{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+(-2){x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,(-2){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must split the coefficient of $-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries \n\n$$\n{a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{(-4)}{2}=-2\n$$\n\nof our matrix. So, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2$ and $b=-2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b=2+(-2)=0.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162595 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161986 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Quadratic Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37bed92b-f672-507f-908f-4180d60967a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355166} {:answer/id #uuid "7a4e148e-4cda-58e5-a8f8-33882e3c14d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355735} {:answer/id #uuid "bdd54d13-8fee-5d25-aa21-73e2fe837e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356326} {:answer/id #uuid "ce4a3363-52f8-53e5-b467-965e5d801060" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356471} {:answer/id #uuid "de2c0735-3990-56ef-921f-e2e38cf38440" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356611}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37bed92b-f672-507f-908f-4180d60967a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355166} :answer-field/id #uuid "24c65efe-f0dc-5833-85bd-c0e38f31a3b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ef8e1919-faae-510c-bb46-8c3989805365" :question/math-academy-id "q-93705" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(-2){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-2){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}(-2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162597 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161987 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2d8b0e0-abf7-5804-b4fc-1492f981e973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160875} {:answer/id #uuid "25c5dc3c-74b1-560e-8928-9a38e10da2d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160876} {:answer/id #uuid "625c16aa-5f30-5dd2-90ef-fdf2417a41f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160877} {:answer/id #uuid "62f64a99-2dff-56c3-9292-977af8cfde01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160878} {:answer/id #uuid "709af0a8-7e72-5eca-b673-1a1761d01bc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160879}] :answer-field/id #uuid "da8601d7-22c5-5de4-8cfd-e028ad48d9e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160874}] :question/id #uuid "cedbc16a-539c-525b-a8a8-cb2cc644cfec" :question/math-academy-id "q-93712" :question/problem "$\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ b & 1\\end{bmatrix}$\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x) = x_{1}^{2} + 8x_{1}x_{2} + x_{2}^{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a + b$?"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357640 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161984 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e62e458d-0724-5dbe-b448-b79404f279f9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices of Quadratic Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d31c7c30-6a09-537a-838e-26380db70980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469674} {:answer/id #uuid "92cf1571-c53f-56df-9ea1-722039f4a649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469675}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92cf1571-c53f-56df-9ea1-722039f4a649" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469675} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5e87bb9-4337-5d11-b331-cb149719d64c" :answer-field/key "T" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470449} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c2b6548-8685-5790-bfe5-2d560d2cc7c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469676} {:answer/id #uuid "db963199-3d93-524d-9ddc-762de74a136c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469677}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db963199-3d93-524d-9ddc-762de74a136c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469677} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccc8546e-485b-59af-b253-732df91bd451" :answer-field/key "U" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470450} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e5a63cd7-c1d9-5588-9330-fe1036e53e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469678} {:answer/id #uuid "c7b3920e-c0f7-5a98-ac0a-e6120f9c52d7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469679}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5a63cd7-c1d9-5588-9330-fe1036e53e50" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469678} :answer-field/id #uuid "431b9dde-c58c-5f17-a803-fb9e8caef06e" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470451}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "93d6f7f1-c1fb-5ae2-b8f7-98ecf5b306a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-94062" :question/problem "Which of the following could be matrices of quadratic forms defined on ${R}^{3}?$\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -8 \\\\ -3 & -8 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,U=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 5 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,V=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that every quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ has an associated $3\\times 3$ symmetric matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $T$ could be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ since it is a $3\\times 3$ symmetric matrix.\n\n- $U$ could also be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ since it is a $3\\times 3$ symmetric matrix.\n\n- $V$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{3}$ since it's a $2\\times 2$ matrix (not $3\\times 3$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$T$ and $U$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357641 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161984 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e62e458d-0724-5dbe-b448-b79404f279f9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices of Quadratic Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "276e7784-3f27-5f16-857d-565398b07228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469680} {:answer/id #uuid "8c5031f6-651d-54a5-875f-0765312ac751" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469681}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "276e7784-3f27-5f16-857d-565398b07228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469680} :answer-field/id #uuid "aaf3a840-0c3e-54a1-a75f-fef852021152" :answer-field/key "D" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470452} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c5ba6a4-f5a4-5d3c-9783-20a15cdf47fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469682} {:answer/id #uuid "bd4c060c-f0ed-573f-9f2e-325a2e5ab7da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469683}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c5ba6a4-f5a4-5d3c-9783-20a15cdf47fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469682} :answer-field/id #uuid "f59b0a79-de63-5dfc-b585-7bed00e3a9b0" :answer-field/key "E" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470453} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b9e0823-8dcb-5fde-8a80-d56b3d3c5c13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469684} {:answer/id #uuid "7d60c142-4a85-5115-8734-c4470d6fadb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469685}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7d60c142-4a85-5115-8734-c4470d6fadb7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186469685} :answer-field/id #uuid "e58d9eb0-2376-5e45-b12e-a50de55ab094" :answer-field/key "F" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186470454}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "61630213-687e-509d-b369-4384ce08371c" :question/math-academy-id "q-94063" :question/problem "Which of the following could be matrices of quadratic forms defined on ${R}^{4}?$\n\n$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 5 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}],\\,E=[\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,F=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 4 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that every quadratic form defined on ${R}^{4}$ has an associated $4\\times 4$ symmetric matrix.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each matrix in turn.\n\n- $D$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{4}.$ Although it's a $4\\times 4$ matrix, $D$ is not symmetric since ${d}_{24}\\ne {d}_{42}.$\n\n- $E$ *cannot* be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{4}$ since it's a $2\\times 2$ matrix (not $4\\times 4$).\n\n- $F$ could be a matrix of a quadratic form defined on ${R}^{4}$ since it is a $4\\times 4$ symmetric matrix.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$F$ only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162616 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161984 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e62e458d-0724-5dbe-b448-b79404f279f9" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Matrices of Quadratic Forms"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97c683e8-d022-5dee-bad9-35e2cd1ccd89" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$H$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160989} {:answer/id #uuid "d9a2f5e8-88f2-5ca7-829a-bde5ff808860" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$H$ and $K$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160990} {:answer/id #uuid "e7a99bd4-fb67-538c-9ece-a4608cb1871a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$J$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160991} {:answer/id #uuid "fca7d285-ba33-51b7-8ce8-27bc0b3b6983" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$J$ and $K$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160992} {:answer/id #uuid "1f4a9a25-8245-5a1f-bdb8-7661bfd56e83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$H$ and $J$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160993}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8bd5c6c9-c655-5a1d-9014-f450a69f1b54" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160988}] :question/id #uuid "6fea8541-6770-5397-b251-59a7fad8f7ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-94065" :question/problem "Which of the following could be matrices of quadratic forms defined on $R^{3}$?\n\n$H = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -4 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}, J = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 8 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 8 & 2 & 6\\end{bmatrix}, K = \\begin{bmatrix}9 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 8 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357647 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161985 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "90f62dc8-396d-5f7f-8295-2e7b5d62bd78" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a4453eb-2267-5b35-a0fa-3451bada2711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354758} {:answer/id #uuid "5ec09201-448a-5927-b1d6-d670c2941e1e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "45" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355501} {:answer/id #uuid "b1417d46-6e5f-553f-91ad-535af69d5276" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "29" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356224} {:answer/id #uuid "da75d9bd-46de-5a72-84a7-b66c5d7f37f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "65" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356586} {:answer/id #uuid "fd8c4557-1921-5623-801b-cbf59ef1f2a3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "50" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356889}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a4453eb-2267-5b35-a0fa-3451bada2711" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "55" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354758} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc3a1765-85b4-55a6-8deb-90bf5ef0fd58" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357286}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "40bf396a-4434-5665-92ca-ca493dc1ea08" :question/math-academy-id "q-94087" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nGiven the matrix $A$ above, evaluate the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}^{T}\\,Ax$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "Substituting $x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ into the expression for $Q(x),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}^{T}\\,Ax \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}14 & 13\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =55.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357651 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161986 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Quadratic Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c31beb4-ab42-57a8-b98e-c38bcfae5c58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}-3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354908} {:answer/id #uuid "8ee2a904-7722-5877-8823-f368265253f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{1}^{2}+4{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355924} {:answer/id #uuid "97920ae7-f871-5bcc-b433-ad7f958e4ab8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355999} {:answer/id #uuid "c4d006dd-514e-5f24-b8ea-65691b567901" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{x}_{1}^{2}-6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356383} {:answer/id #uuid "fd92fbd4-d7d1-557a-8864-0868b5fc986c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd92fbd4-d7d1-557a-8864-0868b5fc986c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356890} :answer-field/id #uuid "c702bda3-b33d-5d6a-b438-e9d3a5575649" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357276}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8b6c5226-6a4c-5905-b982-20f40f90cbd5" :question/math-academy-id "q-94093" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =2{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+(3){x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(3){x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}(3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357654 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161986 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Quadratic Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021bd2b7-706e-57b3-a8af-b3a83db7afce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354673} {:answer/id #uuid "5cd22498-12fa-59db-81fd-6c2ce36f48b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355485} {:answer/id #uuid "b63d5c18-a2a2-5302-9ff5-868dfe95946a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356266} {:answer/id #uuid "f65a1d83-e90e-527d-9df8-022f7c05907b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356809} {:answer/id #uuid "fd26311c-2f18-574d-9496-266fed0c1d74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356885}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b63d5c18-a2a2-5302-9ff5-868dfe95946a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356266} :answer-field/id #uuid "09e70103-bd6b-5347-8799-710e68326fdd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356935}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "96f2319e-e633-542e-b1fa-62302f0afd32" :question/math-academy-id "q-94099" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =2{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+1{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+(-2){x}_{2}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}(2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2})+{x}_{2}({x}_{1}-2{x}_{2})+{x}_{3}(2{x}_{3}) \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{x}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & =2{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}+2{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357656 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161986 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "328b0b77-f789-581e-a119-9823297666ae" :knowledge-point/title "Writing Down a Quadratic Form Given Its Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "074bc0a8-4ace-5935-8132-e8516c14bc11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354727} {:answer/id #uuid "0c35860c-44ad-5b5c-89ff-8920a976c568" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354776} {:answer/id #uuid "29a555f5-45bd-56ad-b133-4ea913d8ef19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355011} {:answer/id #uuid "6211823f-d038-5a7f-841f-e14f57f1ed54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{1}{x}_{3}-3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355538} {:answer/id #uuid "aa727819-380a-594d-a4bd-a5f02c1e6dbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356172}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "074bc0a8-4ace-5935-8132-e8516c14bc11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354727} :answer-field/id #uuid "135db05c-789b-5517-a595-77d2c4b006a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fee716f7-a185-58ac-8ee8-36859424ee03" :question/math-academy-id "q-94105" :question/problem "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $A$ above. Which of the following represents the corresponding quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in terms of the components of $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]?$" :question/worked-solution "**Method 1**\n\nEach entry ${a}_{ij}$ of $A$ corresponds to the term ${a}_{ij}{x}_{i}{x}_{j}$ in the expression of the quadratic form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =1{x}_{1}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}{x}_{2}+(-1){x}_{2}{x}_{3}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{1}+(-1){x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}{x}_{3} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo write down a quadratic form in terms of vector components, we compute the following expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{2} & {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} \\\\ -{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={x}_{1}({x}_{1})+{x}_{2}(2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3})+{x}_{3}(-{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}) \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{2}{x}_{3}-{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+3{x}_{3}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{2}^{2}-2{x}_{2}{x}_{3}+3{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357660 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161987 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02a9e9a8-3c46-5c6f-a0b9-c715263b46fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354679} {:answer/id #uuid "70d8b306-7d64-5a53-bf09-1fcafe21fe9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355662} {:answer/id #uuid "cacc7a23-abd5-5d11-b9dd-14002a05348f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356433} {:answer/id #uuid "cc6a54ea-970f-5bca-8ce6-3a18756c0f41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356448} {:answer/id #uuid "d57fe9de-2cd2-5256-980e-2266baf495ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356534}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cacc7a23-abd5-5d11-b9dd-14002a05348f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356433} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a785e93-2dfe-5d3a-8afd-c6a0e1ac5840" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357165}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6a58c19a-d8e2-5b8b-a8c1-6d0a7f511f7e" :question/math-academy-id "q-94115" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & b \\\\ b & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)=3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}\\,$ is given above. What is the value of $b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =3{x}_{1}^{2}+1{x}_{1}{x}_{2} \\\\  & +\\,1{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+(-2){x}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must split the coefficient of $2{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries \n\n$$\n{a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{2}{2}=1\n$$\n\nof our matrix. So, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $b=1$ and $c=-2.$ Finally, \n\n$$\nb+c=1-2=-1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161987 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eb93c0ea-26d9-5190-9677-b8c7eb6f7ef1" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Matrix of a Quadratic Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26e98748-b388-5506-aac1-9e30f72043d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354991} {:answer/id #uuid "3dd9af0b-3c0e-55a4-a669-bcadc34c08b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355216} {:answer/id #uuid "4978df42-b859-52a6-ba63-1a347384a158" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355314} {:answer/id #uuid "e34d7105-1d3f-5ec1-968a-d5410c870152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356653} {:answer/id #uuid "e64af5fe-d6ac-5ec1-be75-b923dae80e06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356678}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e34d7105-1d3f-5ec1-968a-d5410c870152" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356653} :answer-field/id #uuid "57a91600-a00a-59db-b63e-edcd7437f52e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b751a90c-cbe5-589a-aef5-36f0a41388ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-94120" :question/problem "$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & b \\\\ 6 & a & 0 \\\\ b & 0 & c\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe matrix of the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ is given above. What is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the matrix of the quadratic form must be symmetric, we rewrite our expression as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =1{x}_{1}^{2}+6{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+(-2){x}_{1}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,6{x}_{2}{x}_{1}+1{x}_{2}^{2}+0{x}_{2}{x}_{3} \\\\  & +\\,(-2){x}_{3}{x}_{1}+0{x}_{3}{x}_{2}+0{x}_{3}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that to get a symmetric matrix, we must do the following splits:\n\n- we split the coefficient of $12{x}_{1}{x}_{2}$ between the entries ${a}_{12}={a}_{21}=\\frac{12}{2}=6,$ and\n\n- we split the coefficient of $-4{x}_{1}{x}_{3}$ between the entries ${a}_{13}={a}_{31}=\\frac{-4}{2}=-2.$\n\nSo, the matrix corresponding to our quadratic form is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 6 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,$ $b=-2,$ and $c=0.$ Finally, \n\n$$\na+b+c=1+(-2)+0=-1.\n$$"}]}
